To launch the ec2 instance 

1. create key pair
2. create firewall (security group and inbound rule)
3. import public key to aws account
4. create server and attach public key
5. attach firewall to server

Import a key pair 

Run this in any of the terminal(git bash , putty , superputty , mobixtrem)
ssh-keygen -f <filename>
ssh-keygen -f key - this creates key.pub file and also a key folder(key and key.pub)

Create security group and inbound rule 
Inbound rule : Allow all traffic with IPv4 anywhere
Security group : Allow All ports 

Launch the instance - instance will be in running state (It has 2 IP address : 1 public address and 1 private address )

connect to servers 

Move to the path , where key pair is gerenated 
 ssh -i <private key> user@IP
 ssh -i key ec2-user@public IP



